        "original_id": "b27c96c0-d46f-5af5-9706-bd56a55a1fca",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Roger Miller\n- Songs: \"King of the Road\", \"Dang Me\", \"England Swings\"\n- Roles: singer-songwriter, musician, actor\n- Topics: honky-tonk-influenced novelty songs, Nashville sound era\n\nFacts:\n- Roger Dean Miller, Sr. was born on January 2, 1936, and he was an American singer-songwriter, musician, and actor.\n- Roger Miller was best known for honky-tonk-influenced novelty songs.\n- In November 1964, Roger Miller wrote and originally recorded the song \"King of the Road.\"\n- During the mid-1960s Nashville sound era, Roger Miller had chart-topping country and pop hits with \"King of the Road,\" \"Dang Me,\" and \"England Swings.\"\n- Roger Dean Miller, Sr. died on October 25, 1992.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
